[] 1. What does Elbereth do and what does it stand for and is there any  
[] connetion in all that to the fact that it is also the FTP site at Rutgers?

Elbereth (Star-Queen) is from Tolkien, Lord of the Rings trilogy ...

in the literature, it is known that the mere mention of 'Elbereth' was
enough to drive vile creatures away for awhile.  in NetHack, engraving
'Elbereth' (by various means) has a similar effect.

[] 2. What good are Potions of Water they seem like the most useless items  
[] I have ever found.

they can become potions of holy water or even be used to create
interesting scrolls (under the right circumstances).  potions of
holy water are amongst the most powerful objects in the game ...

[] 3. How does one engage "Wizard" mode on the Mac version of NetHack (3.0)?

rtfm, ... oh you don't have a manual, hmmm ... grab one from
linc.cis.upenn.edu pub/NH3.0/mac/*.doc ...

[] 4. Do you have any sugestions for escaping from demons which have  
[] appeared from a fountain? ( for tht matter is there a way to force them
[] to give you a wish instead of attacking you?)

see 'Elbereth' above ...

you cannot force demons to give you a wish, either they do or don't.

[] 5. How do you get seven wihes from a wand of wishes?

you must understand the concept behind a scroll of charging and also
be lucky and find a wand with 3 wishes in it (try explore-mode for
testing this).

[] 6. Which class is the best to play?

hmmm, perhaps a Priest(ess) for novices.  they can read curses just
by looking at objects.  the other classes are sufficiently different
that you'll have to decide for yourself ...

[] 7. How are you suppposed to get a fire resistance ring?

find it (or play as a Wizard and maybe you'll get one in your starting
inventory).  nobody uses rings anymore since the resistance can also
be gained by eating the right corpses ...

[] 8. What should one play on a musical instrument?

the right tune ...

it is possible to understand this feature just by playing the game
(i.e. thru prayer and oracle consultation) but it should still be
more obvious, IMO.

